From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] variables: don't call FlushVariableNV on sm8250

FlushVariableNV returns EFI_DEVICE_ERROR on sm8250, and every variable call
after it fails until the next boot, so the menu can't read or save the model.
sm8250 commits variables at a reset anyway.

diff --git a/Efi/Qcom.c b/Efi/Qcom.c
index 5feeeb6..e863a1d 100644
--- a/Efi/Qcom.c
+++ b/Efi/Qcom.c
@@ -291,7 +291,11 @@ BOOLEAN
 QcomFlushVariables (OUT EFI_STATUS *Status)
 {
   VARIABLE_SERVICES *Services = Open (&mVariableServicesGuid);
+  QCOM_CHIP          Chip;
 
+  if (QcomChip (&Chip) && !EFI_ERROR (Chip.Id.Status) && Chip.Id.Value == 356) {
+    return FALSE;
+  }
   if (!Services) {
 #ifdef OABL_DEVINFO_SETTINGS
     *Status = VariablesPersistToDevinfo ();
diff --git a/Efi/Qcom.h b/Efi/Qcom.h
index 5a6a797..02f5a55 100644
--- a/Efi/Qcom.h
+++ b/Efi/Qcom.h
@@ -108,10 +108,12 @@ CHAR8 *
 QcomDisplayPanelConfig (VOID);
 
 // Commits NV variables to storage with FlushVariableNV. On SM8750 a
-// variable that isn't flushed is lost at the next reset; SM8250 flushes on
-// ResetSystem but not on a hard reset. SDM845's XBL has no such protocol,
-// so with OABL_DEVINFO_SETTINGS the variables are packed into devinfo
-// instead. Otherwise FALSE without the protocol.
+// variable that isn't flushed is lost at the next reset. SM8250 commits them
+// at a reset, and its FlushVariableNV fails with EFI_DEVICE_ERROR and leaves
+// every variable call failing until the next boot, so it isn't called there
+// (FALSE). SDM845's XBL has no such protocol, so with OABL_DEVINFO_SETTINGS
+// the variables are packed into devinfo instead. Otherwise FALSE without the
+// protocol.
 BOOLEAN
 QcomFlushVariables (OUT EFI_STATUS *Status);
 
